@@ -13,6 +13,16 @@ Two traps this encodes, both paid for on 2026-08-31:
   * A pool figure read at boot is a LOWER BOUND. The pool grows into free VRAM
     as traffic admits experts, until it hits the free-minus-reserve floor.
 
+And one drafter rule: on a slug that pins a drafter to a GPU the drafter emits
+the SAME line shapes as the target -- a second load_tensors model buffer, a
+second KV buffer, a second (smaller) sched_reserve. model, kv and state
+therefore SUM per device; last match wins let a 656 MiB drafter silently
+overwrite the 3,313 MiB target (glm53-flash-dual). compute deliberately stays
+LAST-WINS instead: the target RE-RESERVES after the drafter loads, so summing
+would count the same buffer twice. The drafter's interleaved reservation is
+still dropped into `unaccounted` -- the log does not label which context a
+sched_reserve belongs to, so that one is tracked separately, not guessed at.
+
 Scope: the BYTE split only. Pool slot counts, hit rates and cache health belong to
 CAPTURE: EXPERT CACHE and are deliberately not duplicated here -- one owner per
 number, so the two sections can never disagree.
